Working directory: /tmp/sv-116388ec9bf14d8a928a595dbc264f09/UniversityCourseCatalog

Build a university course catalog Blazor application. Here's everything needed:

1. Create directory `Models/` and add these files:

**Models/Department.cs**
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Department
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

**Models/Course.cs**
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Course
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int DepartmentId { get; set; }
    public string DepartmentName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int Credits { get; set; }
    public string Schedule { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string InstructorName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string InstructorBio { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public bool IsFeatured { get; set; }
}
```

**Models/EnrollmentRequest.cs**
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class EnrollmentRequest
{
    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Name is required.")]
    [StringLength(100)]
    public string StudentName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Student ID is required.")]
    [RegularExpression(@"^[A-Z]{2}\d{6}$", ErrorMessage = "Student ID must be in format: XX000000 (2 letters followed by 6 digits)")]
    public string StudentId { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    [Range(1, int.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    public int CourseId { get; set; }
}
```

2. Create directory `Services/` and add:

**Services/CatalogService.cs** — singleton with in-memory data, 4 departments (CS, Math, Physics, English), 12+ courses, methods: GetDepartmentsAsync(), GetCoursesAsync(string? search, int? departmentId), GetCourseByIdAsync(int id), GetFeaturedCoursesAsync(), SubmitEnrollmentRequestAsync(EnrollmentRequest request) returns bool.

3. Delete `Components/Pages/Counter.razor` and `Components/Pages/Weather.razor`

4. Replace `Components/Pages/Home.razor` with a homepage showing welcome hero, featured courses cards, department links. Route `/`. Static SSR.

5. Create `Components/Pages/Courses.razor` — course catalog with search/filter. Text search input, department dropdown filter, displays courses in list with title/code/department/credits, links to detail. Route `/courses`. Uses `@rendermode InteractiveServer`.

6. Create `Components/Pages/CourseDetail.razor` — full course info page. Route `/courses/{id:int}`. Static SSR.

7. Create `Components/Pages/Enroll.razor` — enrollment form with EditForm, DataAnnotations validation, confirmation message on success. Route `/enroll`. Static SSR (use Enhance for form).

8. Update `Components/Layout/NavMenu.razor` to have Home, Courses, Enroll links (remove Counter/Weather).

9. Update `Program.cs` to register `builder.Services.AddSingleton<UniversityCourseCatalog.Services.CatalogService>();`

10. Replace `wwwroot/app.css` with professional university blue/white CSS styling course cards, search bar, hero section, form.

11. Run `dotnet build` to verify it compiles.

IMPORTANT: The existing project uses .NET 8/9 Blazor with server interactivity. The existing project structure has Components/Layout/ with MainLayout.razor, NavMenu.razor etc. and Components/Pages/ for pages.

For the Enroll page, use `<EditForm Model="@model" OnValidSubmit="HandleSubmit" FormName="enrollment" Enhance>` so it works with static SSR.

For static SSR pages that inject CatalogService, use `@inject` normally. For Courses.razor that uses InteractiveServer, also use `@inject`.

Make sure the _Imports.razor has `@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Models` and `@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Services`.

Here's the current _Imports.razor content to check/update:
The file is at Components/_Imports.razor.

Here's current Program.cs:
```csharp
using UniversityCourseCatalog.Components;

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Add services to the container.
builder.Services.AddRazorComponents()
    .AddInteractiveServerComponents();

var app = builder.Build();

// Configure the HTTP request pipeline.
if (!app.Environment.IsDevelopment())
{
    app.UseExceptionHandler("/Error", createScopeForErrors: true);
    app.UseHsts();
}
app.UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute("/not-found", createScopeForStatusCodePages: true);
app.UseHttpsRedirection();

app.UseAntiforgery();

app.MapStaticAssets();
app.MapRazorComponents<App>()
    .AddInteractiveServerRenderMode();

app.Run();
```

